  "ingredients": [
    "4 (5 ounce) skinless, boneless chicken breast halves",
    "2 tablespoons olive oil",
    "0.5 teaspoon coarse sea salt, or to taste",
    "1 pinch Creole seasoning (such as Tony Chachere's®), or more to taste",
    "1 tablespoon chicken broth, or more to taste"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Z5s08uvHYI2dg5LAd0vwoA47Ngo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240208_simplebakedchickenbreasts_mfs_step1_0181-1-4x3-250b3f145a194aa3bab88e94e3cbae73.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240208/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rub chicken breasts with olive oil and sprinkle both sides with salt and Creole seasoning. Place chicken in a broiler pan.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/JDR_DOQYOzv4-PjXVXxziSlmivQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240208_simplebakedchickenbreasts_mfs_step2_0183-1-4x3-4112183e239b48d9a3698d21b264dc93.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240208/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 10 minutes. Flip chicken and cook until no longer pink in the center and the juices run clear, about 15 minutes more. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/4oUwAICtpf_CCpKcWngZ6q3HOGw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240208_simplebakedchickenbreasts_mfs_step3_0184-1-4x3-58b03143381c48f5baaedeac4fd6bf77.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240208/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove chicken to a plate. Pour chicken broth into the pan and scrape any browned bits off the bottom with a flat-edged wooden spatula. Add more broth if needed to dislodge the browned bits, but not too much or it will be watery.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/QCzOtGHEWfdv1x40g8Sj3DG-HAc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240208_simplebakedchickenbreasts_mfs_step4_0186-1-4x3-efa0e9bf4eef4fe696c5cc9f21969713.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240208/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To serve, drizzle the pan sauce over the chicken.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
